# Citation metadata for Adaptive Cumulative DVH.
# GitHub shows it under "Cite this repository"; Zenodo reads it when it archives a release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Adaptive Cumulative DVH, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "Adaptive Cumulative DVH: cumulative dose evaluation for MR-Linac online adaptive radiotherapy"
abstract: >-
  Adaptive Cumulative DVH is a browser-based tool for evaluating the cumulative dose of
  MR-Linac online adaptive stereotactic body radiotherapy. In this workflow each adapted
  plan is calculated as a full course while only one fraction of it is delivered. The tool
  reads the plan-total DVH export of every fraction, takes the delivered one-fraction share
  of each, and sums the shares over the course (DVH-parameter summation). The cumulative
  values are evaluated against site-specific dose constraints and compared with the
  reference plan and with rigid and deformable dose accumulation. It reads Monaco and
  RayStation DVH exports, covers prostate, liver, lung, pancreas, renal, adrenal, bone and
  stomach treatments, records adapt-to-position or adapt-to-shape for each fraction, and
  keeps a local case archive that can be exported for statistics. All files are processed
  in the browser and nothing is uploaded. Intended for clinical physics review; results
  should be verified against the treatment planning system before any decision.
version: "1.5"
date-released: "2026-11-11"
